Open to any way you or @csmarchbanks think is a reasonable improvement, the sharding calculation has always been a bit over my head.

Maybe either the integral calculation or the overall sharding calculation should weight the delay value more heavily, more like an exponential increase with delay rather than just linear?

```
// When behind we will try to catch up on a proporation of samples per tick.
// This works similarly to an integral accumulator in that pending samples
// is the result of the error integral.
const integralGain = 0.1 / float64(shardUpdateDuration/time.Second)
```
Include delay somewhere in here :point_up:  or here :point_down: ?
```
desiredShards = timePerSample * (dataInRate*dataKeptRatio + integralGain*dataPending)
```
